A new external type has been introduced, mainly for the purpose of output clean artifact during bundling library. The name of this `"module-import"` is referenced from https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/17986#issuecomment-1902096124, but I'm not sure if the current implementation fully meets the intention of this comment. This PR is an incomplete implementation, only implementing the handling of external processing for dynamic imports.

Here's what it does:

Given following config:

```js
// webpack.config.js
externals: {
  path: 'path node-commonjs',
  fs: 'module-import fs',
  'node:fs': 'module-import node:fs',
  'node-fs': 'module-import fs',
},
```

source
```js
it("should allow async externals", async () => {
	const fs1 = await import("fs");
	const fs2 = await import("node:fs");
	const fs3 = await import("node-fs");

	expect(fs1).toStrictEqual(fs2);
	expect(fs1).toStrictEqual(fs3);
});
```

output
```js
var __webpack_exports__ = {};
/*!******************!*\
